  "body": "Under the heading ‘boolean attributes’, an example is given which shows how attributes without an explicit value are given the same value as their name. But according to the parsing algorithm under ‘After attribute name state’, such attributes are actually given an empty string as their value. This corrects the example.\n\n(A grep after `\\b([a-zA-Z])=\"?\\1\"?` shows there are other examples of boolean attributes being explicitly given values matching their names, but I’ve only corrected the example which is incorrect per the parsing algorithm.)\n\nMy name is already in the HTML credits.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6393/common-microsyntaxes.html\" title=\"Last updated on Feb 17, 2021, 5:24 PM UTC (d3b34fa)\">/common-microsyntaxes.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6393/16fbe73...d3b34fa/common-microsyntaxes.html\" title=\"Last updated on Feb 17, 2021, 5:24 PM UTC (d3b34fa)\">diff</a> )",
